From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:09:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 177/190] Sega CD: PRN: on the EXT-port serial link

CONF_WITH_PRINTER_PORT is off on this machine and the stock bconout0
discards every byte, so the desktop's printer icon has always run its
dialog over nothing. The wire it can have is the EXT connector's UART,
which the servant already drives at 4800 8N1 for the serial keyboard,
with GEOS-Genesis's Pico on the far end turning a framed page into PCL.

bconout0 is replaced with one that fills a page and hands the servant
its address; one frame is one page, because the Pico feeds the paper
after a text frame, and a page ends on half a second of silence since
print_file() writes a file's bytes and then simply stops.

The buffer is aligned at run time rather than by the linker: the address
crosses as a 512-byte block index, an alignment attribute says nothing
about where the section lands, and this one landed at 0x2140 while the
servant read from 0x2000.

Not yet working end to end -- see the main tree's commit.
---
 bios/bios.c   |   3 ++
 bios/scdapi.h |   8 +++-
 bios/segacd.c | 119 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 bios/segacd.h |   6 +++
 4 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

